# Local IPOs: an industry area and a unique factory go public as companies of their own (the
# test city has a level-5 oil area and three unique factories). The area's dialog says it is an
# industry area; it is never moved into another building when its main building is lost, and takes
# it back when it stands again. The factory's card in Investments has the factory icon. Needs a
# city with an industry area at level 3+ and a unique factory: the scan logs what it read. Their
# profit is fixed at ₡5,000 a week for the scenario (ipo-site-profit), whatever the city's week was.
# Nothing in the city is touched: lost buildings are only treated as lost.
name local ipos: an industry area and a unique factory list; a lost area waits and gets its home back
local-ipos on
# the city's own counts are set aside and put back at the end: the fixed profit must not count
ipo-forget
ipo-healthy-days 1
ipo-site-profit 500000
ipo-scan
ipo-dialog on
ipo-list-now area
wait 1
expect-visible FinanceOverhaulIpoDialog
expect-text FinanceOverhaulIpoDialogWhere industry area
expect-text FinanceOverhaulIpoDialogLead An industry area your city grew
expect-no-overflow FinanceOverhaulIpoDialog
capture ipo-dialog-area
click FinanceOverhaulIpoDialogClose
ipo-dialog off
pause off
expect-company-site area
expect-company-home same
ipo-lose-home nowhere
expect-company-home lost
ipo-home-back
expect-company-home same
expect-log has its headquarters back
ipo-list-now factory
expect-company-site factory
expect-company-home same
show-economy
wait 1.5
expect-company-first
capture ipo-factory-company
cleanup:
close-economy
ipo-dialog close
ipo-site-profit real
ipo-remove-test
local-ipos restore
